<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brahma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brahma is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> god of creation, who with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> forms the Trimurti. He is usually shown with four faces and four arms, seated on a lotus that rises from the navel of Vishnu. Although he features prominently in myth, he has relatively few temples, and dynasties such as the Pallavas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a> claimed descent from him through epic heroes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brahma.jpg" alt="Brahma" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brahma,_dal_soffitto_del_tempio_di_huchchappaiyya_gudi,_aihole_(balgakot),_karnataka,_VII_secolo_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
